{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p>A certain bowl was sold online for prices varying between <math alttext=\"dollar sign 7\"><mo>$</mo><mn>7</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"dollar sign 13\"><mo>$</mo><mn>13</mn>\n</math>. The number of bowls sold can be modeled by a quadratic function based on the price, where <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> bowls were sold for <math alttext=\"dollar sign 12\"><mo>$</mo><mn>12</mn>\n</math> each and the maximum of <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> bowls were sold for <math alttext=\"dollar sign 10\"><mo>$</mo><mn>10</mn>\n</math> each. According to the model, what is the number of bowls that were sold for <math alttext=\"dollar sign 8\"><mo>$</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math> each?&nbsp;</p>", "keys": ["5"], "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the number of bowls sold can be modeled by a quadratic function based on the price, where a maximum of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> bowls were sold for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 10\"><mo>$</mo><mn>10</mn></math> each&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> bowls were sold for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 12\"><mo>$</mo><mn>12</mn></math> each. This quadratic function can be defined by an equation of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis p minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mi>p</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the number of bowls sold when the price is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign p\"><mo>$</mo><mi>p</mi></math> each, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are constants such that the function reaches its maximum value, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals h\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>. Since the model indicates the maximum number of bowls sold is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> when the price is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 10\"><mo>$</mo><mn>10</mn></math> each, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math> reaches its maximum value, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math>, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals 10\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 9\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals 10\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> in the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis p minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mi>p</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis p minus 10 right parenthesis squared plus 9\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mi>p</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Since the model indicates the number of bowls sold is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> when the price is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 12\"><mo>$</mo><mn>12</mn></math> each, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals 12\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis p minus 10 right parenthesis squared plus 9\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mi>p</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 equals a left parenthesis 12 minus 10 right parenthesis squared plus 9\"><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 equals 4 a plus 9\"><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 4 equals 4 a\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 1 equals a\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Therefore, the model can be represented by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis p right parenthesis equals minus left parenthesis p minus 10 right parenthesis squared plus 9\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mi>p</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis equals minus left parenthesis 8 minus 10 right parenthesis squared plus 9\"><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis equals negative 4 plus 9\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis equals 5\"><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Therefore, according to the model, the number of bowls sold for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 8\"><mo>$</mo><mn>8</mn></math> each was&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "29361323-e4f7-4672-a65d-d394fcdb43c0", "correct_answer": ["5"]}